course: dictionary
lesson: 397
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them show which meaning is meant. Apparatus is one of these. It can mean the tools and machines used for a job, such as beakers in science. It can also mean gym equipment in PE, such as benches, ropes and bars.
explain: Look at the job being done. «Set up the apparatus» in a science lesson means put out the lab equipment. In PE, «get the apparatus out» means fetch the gym equipment. Ask yourself: what is happening here? That tells you which meaning fits.
explain: Apparatus can also mean a system of parts working together, as in «breathing apparatus». Here it is one whole system, not a single tool. Try your meaning in the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: Apparatus means equipment, tools or machines used for a particular job.
fact: In PE, apparatus means gym equipment such as benches, ropes, bars and climbing frames.
fact: «The stay apparatus» is a locking system in a horse's legs that holds it up while it dozes.
fact: Horses can doze standing up, but they still lie down for short times of deep sleep.
fact: Apparatus is a noun, and its plural is apparatuses.
exercise: Pupils had to set up the apparatus for their science experiment. What does apparatus mean here? | A quiet, gloomy feeling | A kind of music played in PE lessons | Gym benches and ropes | *Equipment and tools used for a job, such as beakers and test tubes
exercise: The PE teacher says, «Get the apparatus out.» What does she want the class to fetch? | Lunch boxes for the class | Pencils and rulers | *Benches, ropes and bars from the gym | A whistle for the match
exercise: «The stay apparatus holds the horse up while it dozes.» What is the stay apparatus? | A kind of saddle for riding | *A locking system of parts in the legs that works together | Fizzy drinks in a bottle | A cloud of dust
test: Firefighters wear breathing apparatus. What does apparatus mean in this sentence? | A kind of ladder | The fire engine's siren | Gym benches | *A set of equipment that works together to help them breathe
test: Which word is the plural of apparatus? | apparatuss | apparatus | apparatas | *apparatuses
exam: Which sentence uses apparatus to mean gym equipment? | *«Climb the bars on the apparatus.» | «Put the apparatus in the cupboard.» | «The stay apparatus locks the legs so the horse can doze.» | «Set up the apparatus for the experiment.»
